Subject: Trim the register VM's light call frame setup

What this does
  Building a light frame keeps the variable area's address in a local while
  it fills the slots, instead of storing it in the frame and reading it back
  for every slot, and fills the register file four slots per iteration.
  `call_method` reads the receiver for the callee's `this` after the frame is
  built rather than before, so it no longer stays live across the setup.

Why we need it
  The compiler could not prove the slot stores leave the frame's variable
  pointer unchanged, so it reloaded it per slot, and the early receiver read
  was spilled to the stack and reloaded on every method call. `call_method`
  is the largest single cost on Octane richards and deltablue.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  Skipping the register fill altogether would remove about 5% of the
  instructions on those rows, but the register file is a GC root and a
  popped frame's header words can land under a later frame's registers, so
  every scanned slot must be written on entry.

